  concept: "Authored objective: Loaded Divider Output.\nAuthored requirement: Voltage
    at Vout across parallel R2 and R3 is 2.25-2.45 V. voltage \u2265 2.25 V. voltage
    \u2264 2.45 V. Connection pair R2_Input and R2_Output. Conduction required.\nGeneral
    teaching principle: Resistive division depends on the actual network and any
    connected load; a loaded divider is not the same as an unloaded one.\nOnly fresh,
    authoritative game evidence can establish that this objective is complete."
  analogy: Sharing a resource between branches changes when another load is connected.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: Do not apply an unloaded voltage-divider formula to an arbitrary
    loaded network.
